    "id": "p48-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "Solve\n$$2\\cos x-2\\sin x=\\frac{1}{\\cos x+\\sin x}$$\nfor $0^\\circ\\le x\\le360^\\circ$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=30^\\circ,150^\\circ,210^\\circ,330^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "Since $\\cos x+\\sin x\\ne0$, multiply by the denominator.\n$$\\begin{align*}2(\\cos x-\\sin x)(\\cos x+\\sin x)&=1\\\\2(\\cos^2x-\\sin^2x)&=1\\\\2\\cos2x&=1\\\\\\cos2x&=\\frac12\\\\2x&=60^\\circ,300^\\circ,420^\\circ,660^\\circ\\\\x&=30^\\circ,150^\\circ,210^\\circ,330^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThe denominator is nonzero at each value.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
